D2d1: unwrite a layer's stencil mask where it was written (Lightroom Navigator cut-off)

Lightroom Classic's Develop Navigator thumbnail was whole when Develop opened, then a few seconds
later lost a strip on the right and one at the bottom (GitHub issue Neutron#9).

The Navigator is a 398x318 DC render target. Each frame Lightroom saves its drawing state,
translates by (10,31), pushes a layer masked to a 378x252 path rectangle, draws the thumbnail,
pushes a second layer with the same mask, RESTORES the drawing state, and only then pops both
layers. Our path-mask stencil wrote each mask under the world transform at PushLayer but unwrote
it under the world transform at PopLayer -- by then identity -- so the unwrite landed at
(0,0)-(378,252) instead of (10,31)-(388,283). A 10px strip on the right and a 31px strip at the
bottom stayed promoted. The stencil is not cleared between frames, so on the next frame those
strips failed the mask test and the thumbnail was clipped by exactly its offset. The first frame
after the target is created is always whole, which is why it starts out right.

The layer mask is placed by the world transform in force at PushLayer (as on Windows), so store
the composed maskTransform x world matrix at push and unwrite with that.

Verified with a test program that replays Lightroom's sequence: on 11.10-104 frames 2 and 3 lose
both strips and a masked fill after the pops misses them in the same frame; with the stencil
switched off (NEUTRON_D2D_STENCIL=0) all pass, so the stencil was the cause; with this change all
pass with the stencil on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

--- a/dlls/d2d1/device.c
+++ b/dlls/d2d1/device.c
@@ -3313,8 +3313,11 @@
     return geometry->fill.face_count || geometry->fill.bezier_vertex_count;
 }
 
+/* `transform` is the COMPLETE mask-space -> target transform: the layer's maskTransform composed
+ * with the world transform that was in force at PushLayer. It is deliberately NOT recomputed from
+ * the current world transform -- see d2d_device_context_push_layer_stencil(). */
 static void d2d_device_context_stencil_mask(struct d2d_device_context *context,
-        ID2D1Geometry *mask, const D2D1_MATRIX_3X2_F *mask_transform, int dir)
+        ID2D1Geometry *mask, const D2D1_MATRIX_3X2_F *transform, int dir)
 {
     D2D1_MATRIX_3X2_F saved = context->drawing_state.transform;
     struct d2d_geometry *geometry;
@@ -3322,14 +3325,7 @@
     if (!(geometry = unsafe_impl_from_ID2D1Geometry(mask)))
         return;
 
-    if (mask_transform)
-    {
-        D2D1_MATRIX_3X2_F m = *mask_transform;
-
-        d2d_matrix_multiply(&m, &saved);        /* mask space -> world space */
-        context->drawing_state.transform = m;
-    }
-
+    context->drawing_state.transform = *transform;
     context->stencil_pass = dir;
     d2d_device_context_fill_geometry(context, geometry, NULL, NULL);
     context->stencil_pass = 0;
@@ -3361,6 +3357,7 @@
             && d2d_device_context_ensure_stencil(context))
     {
         unsigned int slot = context->layer_depth;
+        D2D1_MATRIX_3X2_F m = layer_parameters->maskTransform;
         static LONG announced;
 
         /* One line, once per process: a smoke test where this path never runs and one where it
@@ -3371,11 +3368,18 @@
                 "masks now stencilled rather than clipped to their bounds\n",
                 context->pixel_size.width, context->pixel_size.height);
 
-        d2d_device_context_stencil_mask(context, layer_parameters->geometricMask,
-                &layer_parameters->maskTransform, +1);
+        /* The mask is placed by the world transform AT PUSH, and PopLayer must unwrite it in that
+         * same place, so keep the composed matrix rather than the bare maskTransform. Composing
+         * again at PopLayer used whatever transform was current THEN: Lightroom restores its
+         * drawing state (identity) before popping, so the unwrite missed by the translation and
+         * left strips of the mask promoted. The stencil is not cleared between frames, so the
+         * next frame's draws failed the test there -- the Develop Navigator thumbnail clipped by
+         * exactly its (10,31) offset (GitHub Neutron#9). */
+        d2d_matrix_multiply(&m, &context->drawing_state.transform);   /* mask space -> target */
+        d2d_device_context_stencil_mask(context, layer_parameters->geometricMask, &m, +1);
         context->stencil_mask[slot] = layer_parameters->geometricMask;
         ID2D1Geometry_AddRef(context->stencil_mask[slot]);
-        context->stencil_mask_transform[slot] = layer_parameters->maskTransform;
+        context->stencil_mask_transform[slot] = m;
         context->layer_stencilled[slot] = 1;
         ++context->stencil_depth;
         stencilled = TRUE;
@@ -3457,7 +3461,8 @@
     if (context->layer_depth)
         --context->layer_depth;
 
-    /* NEUTRON PATH-MASK STENCIL: unwrite exactly the geometry this layer wrote. */
+    /* NEUTRON PATH-MASK STENCIL: unwrite exactly the geometry this layer wrote, where it wrote
+     * it -- under the transform stored at PushLayer, not the current one. */
     if (context->layer_depth < ARRAY_SIZE(context->layer_stencilled)
             && context->layer_stencilled[context->layer_depth])
     {
